statement:
You are given an integer array `nums` indexed from 0. Every interior index `i` (that is, `1 <= i <= nums.length - 2`) gets a beauty score:

- **2** when `nums[i]` is strictly larger than every element to its left and strictly smaller than every element to its right;
- otherwise **1** when it is strictly between its two neighbours, `nums[i - 1] < nums[i] < nums[i + 1]`;
- otherwise **0**.

Return the total of the beauty scores over all interior indices. The first and last indices are not scored.

validator:
function validate([nums]) {
  if (!Array.isArray(nums) || nums.length < 3 || nums.length > 100000) return 'nums needs 3 to 100000 values.';
  if (nums.some(v => !Number.isInteger(v) || v < 1 || v > 100000)) return 'Each value is an integer from 1 to 100000.';
  return null;
}

